{"kind":"artifact","text":"The four repaired pages at exact clean head d7a41b0c99b4d52a48830d3e75471915f59c3516 (branch request/citation-reanchor-fd0680ef), answering request ec602a2f under promise bad4f71f. This artifact is the implementation report.\n\nWhat was asked and what was done. Four citations of retired UI artifact fd0680ef now name its live successor 6e37840d, ui at main commit 33c29b1e. The chain from fd0680ef runs 7a3f0694, 85d8cf5c, 39d573ac to 6e37840d, and I walked it rather than guessing a target.\n\nWhat I did beyond the literal ask, and why. Moving a citation onto a newer artifact asserts that the page describes that artifact's world, so I read each page's UI claims at commit 33c29b1e instead of substituting a string. Two pages no longer described anything true, and re-anchoring them unchanged would have made the log assert a falsehood freshly rather than leave one standing.\n\ndocs/reference/limits.md claimed the browser's commit graph is a newest-80 window and that the view says \"Showing the newest 80 commits.\" Nothing draws that graph. api.graph() in ui/src/lib/api.ts has no caller anywhere in ui/, and ui/src/lib/store.ts records the poll as removed with the surface that read it. The resident does still cap at 80 and mark the response truncated, at internal/service/ui.go:60, with a test at server_test.go:537, and /v0/graph is still routed. The section now states the endpoint's bound and says nothing displays it, and the page cites internal/service for what is now a server-side claim.\n\ndocs/reference/gs/serve.md claimed the browser view reports local checkout state - basenames, branch, HEAD, and clean, dirty, detached, bare, locked, prunable or unavailable. The browser reads only local.repo from /v0/worktrees, at ui/src/lib/store.ts:40, and discards the rest. The endpoint still emits all of it, and that disclosure is what the section's loopback-safety argument is actually about, so the claim is attributed to the endpoint with the browser's narrower use stated.\n\ndocs/concepts/components.md and docs/reference/mcp/presence.md were checked the same way and hold: the resident serves the committed build rather than ui/src, which make ui-check enforces, and the focus union is still capped at eight events at ui/src/lib/interaction.ts:242.\n\nLeft alone deliberately: the dead api.graph() fetcher. Deleting it changes UI source and needs its own lane with a rebuilt embed, so it does not belong in a documentation head.\n\nGates at this exact head: make docs passes, git diff --check clean. The gate was green before the change as well, so I did not treat green as evidence - pointing one citation at a nonexistent artifact makes internal/docset fail, which is what shows the gate reads these front matters. internal/docset/citation_baseline.txt is unchanged and correctly so: its four entries are branch-name artifacts, a different defect class, and none of the four repaired citations was ever on it.\n\nRecorded in assert ec160569 and not fixed here: 158 of 200 documentation citations point at retired artifacts and 53 of 57 citing documents are flared. None of these four documents becomes unflared by this repair - components.md goes from 8 bad citations to 7. The work is correct and changes nothing anybody can see. That backlog needs its own request.\n\nOne consequence for the merge queue. My open UI lane at ac2dd80f will, if it merges, retire 6e37840d and publish a successor at ui, re-flaring these same four pages. Whoever merges that head should repoint them again in the same step.","body":{"commit":"d7a41b0c99b4d52a48830d3e75471915f59c3516","path":"docs"}}